WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.950
Small Talk and Networking.

2
00:00:02.230 --> 00:00:06.774
Day 22 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the Communication phase.

3
00:00:08.524 --> 00:00:09.548
The key idea.

4
00:00:09.828 --> 00:00:12.623
Small talk is how people start to trust each other.

5
00:00:12.903 --> 00:00:17.852
Most opportunities (jobs, partnerships, mentors) start with a 3-minute chat.

6
00:00:18.132 --> 00:00:19.668
Ask, listen, follow up.

7
00:00:21.018 --> 00:00:21.871
Part 1.

8
00:00:22.151 --> 00:00:23.709
The 4-step conversation.

9
00:00:24.959 --> 00:00:25.876
Step 1:

10
00:00:26.156 --> 00:00:28.567
Open: comment on the shared situation.

11
00:00:28.847 --> 00:00:29.764
Step 2:

12
00:00:30.044 --> 00:00:32.071
Ask: open questions about them.

13
00:00:32.351 --> 00:00:33.268
Step 3:

14
00:00:33.548 --> 00:00:36.129
Connect: find something in common, share a little.

15
00:00:36.409 --> 00:00:37.369
Step 4:

16
00:00:37.649 --> 00:00:39.719
Exit: gracefully, with a next step.

17
00:00:41.069 --> 00:00:41.943
Part 2.

18
00:00:42.223 --> 00:00:43.119
Openers.

19
00:00:44.369 --> 00:00:45.649
Conference or meetup.

20
00:00:45.929 --> 00:00:47.081
Hi, I'm Ashish.

21
00:00:47.361 --> 00:00:48.833
What did you think of that talk?

22
00:00:49.113 --> 00:00:50.564
What brings you here today?

23
00:00:50.844 --> 00:00:52.913
Is this your first time at this conference?

24
00:00:54.263 --> 00:00:55.586
Office or new team.

25
00:00:55.866 --> 00:00:57.466
Hi, I don't think we've met.

26
00:00:57.746 --> 00:00:59.922
I'm Ashish, I work on the checkout team.

27
00:01:00.202 --> 00:01:01.418
How was your weekend?

28
00:01:01.698 --> 00:01:04.066
Are you working on anything exciting this quarter?

29
00:01:05.416 --> 00:01:07.293
Travel (airport, train, flight).

30
00:01:07.573 --> 00:01:09.643
Are you travelling for work or holiday?

31
00:01:09.923 --> 00:01:11.800
Have you been to Singapore before?

32
00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:12.997
Any tips?

33
00:01:13.277 --> 00:01:15.048
This delay is long, isn't it?

34
00:01:15.328 --> 00:01:16.437
Where are you heading?

35
00:01:17.787 --> 00:01:19.494
Waiting or lift or café.

36
00:01:19.774 --> 00:01:21.481
Busy day today, isn't it?

37
00:01:21.761 --> 00:01:22.955
That smells great.

38
00:01:23.235 --> 00:01:24.323
What did you order?

39
00:01:25.673 --> 00:01:26.569
Part 3.

40
00:01:26.849 --> 00:01:28.769
Keep it going: the FORD topics.

41
00:01:30.019 --> 00:01:31.385
Here is a quick table:

42
00:01:31.665 --> 00:01:32.966
Topic, and Question.

43
00:01:33.246 --> 00:01:34.419
Family or home:

44
00:01:34.699 --> 00:01:36.577
Are you from Bangalore originally?

45
00:01:36.857 --> 00:01:37.838
Occupation:

46
00:01:38.118 --> 00:01:41.531
What kind of work do you do? then What do you enjoy most about it?

47
00:01:41.811 --> 00:01:42.878
Recreation:

48
00:01:43.158 --> 00:01:44.865
What do you do when you're not working?

49
00:01:45.145 --> 00:01:45.977
Dreams:

50
00:01:46.257 --> 00:01:47.963
What are you excited about this year?

51
00:01:49.313 --> 00:01:50.999
Follow-up magic phrases:

52
00:01:51.279 --> 00:01:52.921
Oh, how did you get into that?

53
00:01:53.201 --> 00:01:55.015
That's interesting, tell me more.

54
00:01:55.295 --> 00:01:56.340
What was that like?

55
00:01:57.690 --> 00:01:58.607
Part 4.

56
00:01:58.887 --> 00:02:01.063
Introduce yourself (networking pitch).

57
00:02:02.313 --> 00:02:03.252
You could say:

58
00:02:03.532 --> 00:02:04.449
I'm Ashish.

59
00:02:04.729 --> 00:02:08.185
I'm a backend engineer working on a grocery marketplace.

60
00:02:08.465 --> 00:02:10.833
Lots of Kafka and microservices.

61
00:02:11.113 --> 00:02:15.572
Lately I've been figuring out how to make checkout reliable during flash sales.

62
00:02:15.852 --> 00:02:16.855
What about you?

63
00:02:18.205 --> 00:02:21.895
Keep it short and interesting, and end with a question back to them.

64
00:02:23.245 --> 00:02:24.205
Part 5.

65
00:02:24.485 --> 00:02:25.765
Exiting politely.

66
00:02:27.015 --> 00:02:28.487
It was great talking to you.

67
00:02:28.767 --> 00:02:31.413
I'm going to grab a coffee before the next session.

68
00:02:31.693 --> 00:02:33.015
I don't want to keep you.

69
00:02:33.295 --> 00:02:34.810
Can we connect on LinkedIn?

70
00:02:35.090 --> 00:02:36.669
Let me introduce you to Priya.

71
00:02:36.949 --> 00:02:38.698
She's working on exactly that.

72
00:02:40.048 --> 00:02:40.987
Part 6.

73
00:02:41.267 --> 00:02:43.251
Follow up within 24 hours.

74
00:02:44.501 --> 00:02:46.378
Here is a template you can copy.

75
00:02:46.658 --> 00:02:49.965
Hi Neha, great meeting you at the Kafka Summit yesterday!

76
00:02:50.245 --> 00:02:53.317
I really enjoyed our chat. about. consumer lag.

77
00:02:53.597 --> 00:02:56.050
Here's the blog post I mentioned: link.

78
00:02:56.330 --> 00:02:57.866
Would love to stay in touch.

79
00:02:58.146 --> 00:02:58.978
Ashish.

80
00:03:01.828 --> 00:03:02.767
Part 7.

81
00:03:03.047 --> 00:03:05.671
Topics to avoid with strangers or at work.

82
00:03:06.921 --> 00:03:11.401
Politics, religion, salary, weight or appearance, gossip about colleagues.

83
00:03:12.751 --> 00:03:13.625
Part 8.

84
00:03:13.905 --> 00:03:15.335
Practice conversations.

85
00:03:16.585 --> 00:03:17.673
At a tech meetup.

86
00:03:17.953 --> 00:03:19.979
Here is how the conversation goes.

87
00:03:20.259 --> 00:03:21.667
Hi, I'm Ashish.

88
00:03:21.947 --> 00:03:24.593
That was a great talk on Kafka, wasn't it?

89
00:03:24.873 --> 00:03:26.089
Hi, I'm Neha.

90
00:03:26.369 --> 00:03:27.222
Yes!

91
00:03:27.502 --> 00:03:30.041
The part about consumer lag was really useful.

92
00:03:30.321 --> 00:03:32.433
Are you working with Kafka at the moment?

93
00:03:32.713 --> 00:03:35.145
Yes, we use it for payments at my company.

94
00:03:35.425 --> 00:03:36.534
What about you?

95
00:03:36.814 --> 00:03:37.603
Same.

96
00:03:37.883 --> 00:03:40.977
We use it for order events in a grocery app.

97
00:03:41.257 --> 00:03:43.518
How long have you been working on payments?

98
00:03:44.868 --> 00:03:46.468
The conversation continues.

99
00:03:46.748 --> 00:03:47.985
About four years.

100
00:03:48.265 --> 00:03:49.972
Before that I was in banking.

101
00:03:50.252 --> 00:03:51.255
Interesting!

102
00:03:51.535 --> 00:03:52.815
What made you switch?

103
00:03:53.095 --> 00:03:55.676
I wanted to build products, not just maintain them.

104
00:03:55.956 --> 00:03:57.129
That makes sense.

105
00:03:57.409 --> 00:03:59.543
Would you like to connect on LinkedIn?

106
00:03:59.823 --> 00:04:01.551
I'd love to stay in touch.

107
00:04:01.831 --> 00:04:03.580
Sure, here's my QR code.

108
00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:06.530
The conversation continues.

109
00:04:06.810 --> 00:04:07.557
Great.

110
00:04:07.837 --> 00:04:09.991
It was really nice meeting you, Neha.

111
00:04:10.271 --> 00:04:12.127
Enjoy the rest of the event!

112
00:04:13.477 --> 00:04:14.907
In the lift at the office.

113
00:04:15.187 --> 00:04:17.213
Here is how the conversation goes.

114
00:04:17.493 --> 00:04:18.581
Morning!

115
00:04:18.861 --> 00:04:19.843
Busy day?

116
00:04:20.123 --> 00:04:20.997
Morning!

117
00:04:21.277 --> 00:04:22.963
Yes, we have a release today.

118
00:04:23.243 --> 00:04:24.523
How about you?

119
00:04:24.803 --> 00:04:25.784
Same here.

120
00:04:26.064 --> 00:04:27.323
Lots of meetings.

121
00:04:27.603 --> 00:04:29.203
Did you have a good weekend?

122
00:04:29.483 --> 00:04:31.211
Yes, I went to Nandi Hills.

123
00:04:31.491 --> 00:04:33.155
The sunrise was beautiful.

124
00:04:34.505 --> 00:04:36.105
The conversation continues.

125
00:04:36.385 --> 00:04:37.174
Nice!

126
00:04:37.454 --> 00:04:39.203
I've always wanted to go.

127
00:04:39.483 --> 00:04:40.785
Is it crowded?

128
00:04:41.065 --> 00:04:43.155
Go early, before 5, and it's fine.

129
00:04:43.435 --> 00:04:44.374
Good tip.

130
00:04:44.654 --> 00:04:45.849
Have a good day!

131
00:04:46.129 --> 00:04:47.174
You too!

132
00:04:48.524 --> 00:04:50.060
That's the end of this lesson.

133
00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:55.012
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

134
00:04:55.292 --> 00:05:01.393
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

